# EXAMPLE TEMPLATE -- do not put a real credential, ID, or hostname in this
# file. Every value below must be empty or an obviously-fake placeholder; a
# CI gate (scripts/check-example-file-leaks.sh) rejects any `.example` file
# containing a real-looking secret/ID pattern (cmd_829).
#
# GCP (Cloud Run) deployment configuration for consumer apps generated from
# this repo (app-generator) -- used by scripts/gcp-env.sh / gcp-setup.sh /
# gcp-deploy.sh / gcp-seed.sh / gcp-teardown.sh. This is a separate,
# unrelated deployment path from Vercel (.env.vercel.production.local.example)
# -- see docs/knowledge/vercel-deploy-scripts-canonical-source.md. Both paths
# read the SAME .env.production.local file at this repo's root, so the two
# templates below intentionally overlap on Neon/Auth.js/Upstash/seed keys.
# Canonical copy -- consumer repos reference this file via their
# app-generator submodule rather than keeping their own duplicate (same
# pattern as .env.vercel.production.local.example, cmd_711).
# Copy this file to .env.production.local and fill in the actual values.
# Never commit .env.production.local (it is gitignored via .env* in .gitignore).

# ── GCP project ───────────────────────────────────────────
# If left blank, gcp-env.sh falls back to the ambient `gcloud config
# get-value project` and prints a WARNING naming which project it picked --
# set this explicitly to avoid depending on whatever project happens to be
# active in the local gcloud CLI state.
PROJECT_ID=
# Optional -- defaults shown are gcp-env.sh's own fallback values.
REGION=asia-northeast1
SERVICE_NAME=app
SA_NAME=app-cloud-run-sa
REPO_NAME=app-generator

# ── Neon Postgres ──────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL = pooled (PgBouncer) endpoint, for app runtime queries.
# DIRECT_URL   = unpooled endpoint, used only by the migrate Job's
#   `prisma migrate deploy` -- see docs/knowledge/prisma-direct-vs-pooled-connection.md.
# This script does not provision Neon itself. If a Vercel deployment for the
# same app was already set up (scripts/vercel-setup.sh), leave both of these
# blank: gcp-env.sh automatically reuses DATABASE_URL_PROD /
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED_PROD from this same file. Otherwise obtain both from
# the Neon console, or run scripts/vercel-setup.sh first to get-or-create the
# Neon project automatically.
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_URL=

# ── Auth.js ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# generate-once-persist: auto-generated on first run and written back to
# .env.production.local if left blank -- keep fixed thereafter.
AUTH_SECRET=

# ── Upstash Redis ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by gcp-setup.sh Step 4.5 to auto-create the Redis DB via the Upstash
# Management API. Obtain from https://console.upstash.com/account/api.
UPSTASH_EMAIL=
UPSTASH_API_KEY=
# Optional -- AWS-style region name for the Upstash global DB primary region.
UPSTASH_PRIMARY_REGION=ap-northeast-1

# ── Seed baseline admin ────────────────────────────────────
# The bootstrap admin login the app-migrate Job's `npm run db:seed-baseline`
# creates -- an operator's actual admin login, not a random secret. See
# docs/knowledge/seed-baseline-credential-hardening.md.
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ── Prisma Accelerate (optional, off by default) ───────────
# Unrelated to the Cloud SQL->Neon reconnection; see gcp-deploy.sh's commented
# -out Accelerate block and docs/knowledge/manual-ops.md §1 to revive it.
PRISMA_ACCELERATE_API_KEY=

# ── Prisma connection pool cap (optional, off by default) ──
# Leave blank for the default deploy target (Neon's pooled endpoint) --
# lib/prisma-pool.ts's own default (5) already fits that shape. Set to 2
# only if DATABASE_URL above points at a direct/unpooled connection instead
# (e.g. a self-managed Cloud SQL instance) -- see
# docs/knowledge/prisma-pool-max-tuning.md. gcp-deploy.sh forwards this to
# the deployed Cloud Run service only when set.
PRISMA_POOL_MAX=
